 "id": "vision_identity_seam",
 "version": "1.0.0",
 "depends_on": [
  "shape_decode_loop"
 ],
 "description": "THE PERCEPT->IDENTITY SEAM, arm B (VISION_IDENTITY_SEAM_PREREG.md, seeds 72000-72999). A region recognised in one frame is decided to be THE SAME HELD IDENTITY in the next -- or, if the graph cannot tell it from noise, it is minted as a new one and the codebook grows. Keeps the sd loop's topology and replaces only the recognition verdict: V3 normalized cross-correlation against a MEASURED noise floor, in place of `Count(residual)==0` over a compositional decode. SHIPS OFF (IdentitySeamParams.seam = 0.0) and is not in any default boot set, so every committed result reproduces byte-identically (section 9). No new Rust, no new Term, and NO NUMERIC THRESHOLD anywhere.",
 "nodes": [
